{
  "name": "cloud_volume_bake",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§25e: the cloud bakes moved off the loading screen (issue #144). WHAT THIS HAS TO PROVE IS THAT NOTHING MOVED ON SCREEN. The volume is baked on a background thread and split across cores now, and the offline suite pins the bytes as identical band for band -- but identical bytes reach the GPU through a different path: the texture is uploaded on the first main-thread frame that asks for it rather than in the static constructor, and until that happens Available answers false and CloudSheetOverlay draws §25b. A run that captured one frame too early would show the baked atlas, which is a plausible-looking cloudy sky and the wrong renderer. So cloud_volume_shader is pinned at 1 beside cloud_volume_baked, and the frame is compared against the same scenario on main at ΔE. SETUP IS cloud_volume_ab's, TERM FOR TERM, because that is the frame the ΔE is against. Low but positive sun so the march has something to self-shadow, overcast so §25's sheets are large and few, and cloud_view_coverage pinned so a frame with no cloud in it fails rather than reporting a confident zero difference between two empty skies.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "SetTile",
      "args": {
        "latitude": "45"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetSeason",
      "args": {
        "dayOfYear": "40"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "realistic_preset",
        "enabled": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetWeather",
      "args": {
        "weatherDef": "Clear",
        "instant": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "cloud_cover_forced_overcast",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "cloud_sheet",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "cloud_volume",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTime",
      "args": {
        "hour": "19.60"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "sun_elevation",
        "expectedValue": "8.5732",
        "tolerance": "0.05"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "cloud_volume_format",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0.001"
      }
    },
    {
